* =====================================================================================================
* ti/tps61040 view "boost" (breadboard.dev, Apache-2.0): TI TPS61040 boost converter, AVERAGED: its input
* current and start-up surge, a `pi` power view (ADR-009 D2 rule 3: switching converters are averaged).
* Datasheet-fitted from SLVS413L (October 2002, revised August 2026), sections 5.5, 6.3 and 6.4; none of
* the dial-me-spinner suite's models is used.  Phase 2 P0's spike view, packaged in P1 with its output
* made internal (below).  Written to ADR-009 D2's rules: I-type B sources of node voltages only,
* two-argument min()/max(), internal signals as I-type sources into 1 Ohm.
*
* SLVS413L figures:
*   VUVLO 1.5 V typ / 1.7 V max (5.5); EN VIH 1.3 V min, VIL 0.4 V max; IQ 28 uA typ (not switching),
*     ISD 0.1 uA typ                                                         -> uvlo, iq, isd
*   switch current limit ILIM 350 / 400 / 450 mA; Ipeak = ILIM + VIN/L x 100 ns (6.3.1, Eq. 1) -> ilim
*   minimum off time 250 / 400 / 550 ns; maximum on time 4 / 6 / 7.5 us (5.5)   -> toffmin, tonmax
*   PFM (6.4.1): the switch turns on while VFB < VREF (1.233 V typ), off at Ipeak or the maximum on
*     time, and stays off for at least toffmin
*   soft start (6.3.2): current limit ILIM/4 for 256 cycles, ILIM/2 for the next 256, then ILIM
* The average of one switching cycle, from those rules: on time ton = L Ipk / VIN (at most tonmax),
*   fall time tf = L Ipk / VD with VD = VOUT + vdf - VSW the off-time inductor voltage; if tf <=
*   toffmin the cycle is discontinuous (Iavg = Ipk/2 (ton + tf)/(ton + toffmin), period ton +
*   toffmin), otherwise the next cycle starts at Ipk - VD toffmin / L (Iavg = Ipk - VD toffmin/(2 L),
*   period VD toffmin / VIN + toffmin). The two forms meet at tf = toffmin.
*
* THE OUTPUT IS THE VIEW'S OWN STATE.  An averaged boost cannot deliver its energy through the board's
*   rectifier (at DC the inductor holds SW at VIN, below the output), and a view's ports are the
*   package's pins (spec/package.md section 3), none of which is the output.  So the converter's output
*   is an internal node: its capacitance `cout`, its load `rload` and its regulation target `vout`
*   (VREF times the board's feedback divider) are instance parameters, which the board sets.  The
*   averaged power, eta x P_in, is delivered into it, and the regulation gate (PFM stops at VREF) reads
*   it.  It starts from the precharge the board's inductor and rectifier give it (VIN - vdf), which the
*   board's own parts carry.  The board's output net is NOT driven by this view: only the input
*   current (drawn at SW, through the board's inductor) and the start-up surge are modelled.
* ASSUMPTIONS: efficiency eta = 0.85 (inside Figures 5-1..5-4, not fitted); vdf = 0.4 V, the
*   rectifier's forward drop at the start-up currents; the UVLO hysteresis 50 mV (none is given);
*   the EN switch centred at 0.85 V; the averaged current filtered with 2 us; the regulation fades
*   the average over a 30 mV FB band below VREF (a proportional stand-in for the PFM loop); the
*   soft-start steps smoothed over 4 cycles; the cycle counter V(tbnc) = cycles / 1000; a damping
*   resistance rdamp = 1 kOhm from SW to VIN (Phase 2 P5): when the converter stops (EN low, or VIN
*   below UVLO, as a brown-out's reset does), the board's inductor and the rectifier's capacitance at
*   SW ring at several MHz, which the switching losses of the real part damp within a few cycles; an
*   averaged view has no such losses, so undamped the ringing held ngspice at nanosecond steps (W2's
*   reset: 72 s for 2 ms). Across the inductor it carries |V(SW) - V(VIN)| / rdamp, which is L di/dt
*   / rdamp of the averaged current: below 1 mA, under 1 % of the averaged current at start-up.
* NOT modelled: switching ripple, the regulation loop's dynamics and accuracy, IFB, thermal
*   shutdown, RDS(on) loss (in eta), SW leakage, the board's output net (above).
*
* Ports: VIN SW FB EN GNDP (the package's pins; GND renamed GNDP, spec/package.md section 5).
* =====================================================================================================
.subckt TI_TPS61040_BOOST_AVG VIN SW FB EN GNDP params: lind=10u ilim=0.4 toffmin=400n tonmax=6u
+ uvlo=1.5 uvlo_hys=0.05 iq=28u isd=0.1u eta=0.85 vdf=0.4 tfilt=2u vout=13 cout=1u rload=1Meg rdamp=1k
* enable (EN high) and UVLO with hysteresis: V(tben), V(tbuv) = 0..1
B_EN    GNDP tben I = 0.5 + 0.5*tanh((V(EN,GNDP) - 0.85)/0.02)
R_EN    tben GNDP 1
B_UV    GNDP tbuv I = 0.5 + 0.5*tanh((V(VIN,GNDP) - {uvlo} + {uvlo_hys}*V(tbuv,GNDP))/0.005)
R_UV    tbuv GNDP 1
C_UV    tbuv GNDP 10n
* soft-start factor from the cycle counter: 0.25, 0.5, then 1
B_SS    GNDP tbss I = 0.25 + 0.125*(1 + tanh((V(tbnc,GNDP) - 0.256)/0.004))
+                   + 0.25*(1 + tanh((V(tbnc,GNDP) - 0.512)/0.004))
R_SS    tbss GNDP 1
* clamped inductor voltages (divisors): on-time VIN, off-time VD (against the view's own output)
B_VI    GNDP tbvi I = min(max(V(VIN,GNDP), 0.3), 10)
R_VI    tbvi GNDP 1
B_VD    GNDP tbvd I = min(max(V(tbvo,GNDP) + {vdf} - V(SW,GNDP), 0.02), 40)
R_VD    tbvd GNDP 1
* peak current and on time (ton in us, Ipk in A)
B_TON   GNDP tbton I = 1e6*min({tonmax}, {lind}*({ilim}*V(tbss,GNDP) + V(tbvi,GNDP)/{lind}*100n)/max(V(tbvi,GNDP),0.3))
R_TON   tbton GNDP 1
B_IPK   GNDP tbipk I = 1e-6*V(tbton,GNDP)*V(tbvi,GNDP)/{lind}
R_IPK   tbipk GNDP 1
* fall time (us), then the cycle's average current (A) and period (us)
B_TF    GNDP tbtf I = 1e6*{lind}*V(tbipk,GNDP)/max(V(tbvd,GNDP),0.02)
R_TF    tbtf GNDP 1
B_IAV   GNDP tbiav I = V(tbtf,GNDP) <= 1e6*{toffmin}
+                     ? V(tbipk,GNDP)/2*(V(tbton,GNDP) + V(tbtf,GNDP))/(V(tbton,GNDP) + 1e6*{toffmin})
+                     : V(tbipk,GNDP) - V(tbvd,GNDP)*{toffmin}/(2*{lind})
R_IAV   tbiav GNDP 1
B_TC    GNDP tbtc I = V(tbtf,GNDP) <= 1e6*{toffmin}
+                    ? V(tbton,GNDP) + 1e6*{toffmin}
+                    : 1e6*(V(tbvd,GNDP)*{toffmin}/max(V(tbvi,GNDP),0.3) + {toffmin})
R_TC    tbtc GNDP 1
* regulation gate (PFM stops at VREF: the output at vout), over the output's equivalent of 30 mV at FB
B_GR    GNDP tbgr I = min(1, max(0, ({vout} - V(tbvo,GNDP))/(0.03*{vout}/1.233)))
R_GR    tbgr GNDP 1
B_IT    GNDP tbit I = V(tben,GNDP)*V(tbuv,GNDP)*V(tbgr,GNDP)*V(tbiav,GNDP)
R_IT    tbit GNDP 1
B_ITF   GNDP tbif I = V(tbit,GNDP)
R_ITF   tbif GNDP 1
C_ITF   tbif GNDP {tfilt}
* cycle counter: integrates the switching frequency while enabled (1 nF: 1e-12 A per Hz gives
* 1 mV per cycle), discharged while disabled
B_NC    GNDP tbnc I = V(tben,GNDP)*V(tbuv,GNDP)*V(tbgr,GNDP)*1e-6/min(max(V(tbtc,GNDP), 0.1), 1000)
B_NCR   tbnc GNDP I = (1 - V(tben,GNDP)*V(tbuv,GNDP))*V(tbnc,GNDP)/1k
C_NC    tbnc GNDP 1n
R_NC    tbnc GNDP 1G
* the averaged switch: the inductor current drawn at SW
B_SW    SW GNDP I = V(tbif,GNDP)*min(1, max(0, V(SW,GNDP)/0.3))
* the converter's own output (header): the delivered power eta x P_in, the precharge the board's
* inductor and rectifier give it (no current drawn: they are the board's), its capacitance and load
B_OUT   GNDP tbvo I = min(V(tbif,GNDP)*min(1, max(0, V(SW,GNDP)/0.3)),
+                  {eta}*min(max(V(SW,GNDP), 0), 10)*V(tbif,GNDP)*min(1, max(0, V(SW,GNDP)/0.3))
+                  /min(max(V(tbvo,GNDP), 0.5), 40))
B_PRE   GNDP tbvo I = max(0, V(VIN,GNDP) - {vdf} - V(tbvo,GNDP))
C_VO    tbvo GNDP {cout}
R_VO    tbvo GNDP {rload}
B_IQ    VIN GNDP I = ({iq}*V(tben,GNDP) + {isd}*(1 - V(tben,GNDP)))*min(1, max(0, V(VIN,GNDP)/1.5))
R_FB    FB GNDP 1G
* the SW node's damping (header)
R_DAMP  SW VIN {rdamp}
.ends TI_TPS61040_BOOST_AVG
